    "alpha_curve_units": "Normalized [time,alpha] keyframes, linearly interpolated; multiply texture alpha by curve value.",
    "blend": "Use Godot CanvasItem additive blending for add, standard alpha blending for mix. Multiply RGB by hex color. For particles, use particle_blend_by_texture when present; otherwise inherit parent blend. Paths are repository relative; prefix res:// when loading in Godot.",
    "particles": "Optional particles emit once at t=0 from the same origin; amount is total count. Choose speed and scale uniformly within their ranges, angle uniformly in a cone centered on up (-90 degrees), spread_deg is full cone width; 360 means all directions. Initial rotation uniform [0,360), held constant. Integrate gravity, retain initial scale, and linearly fade alpha from 1 to 0 across lifetime. Omitted particles means none.",
    "feedback": "Missing screen_shake/hit_stop means zero. Shake lasts 0.16 seconds, updates at 30 Hz with random x/y in [-amplitude,+amplitude] times (1-t/0.16), then returns to base camera. Pause gameplay and actor animation during hit_stop, but let VFX and camera run in real time; UI remains responsive.",
    "limits": "For effects/events in the same 80 ms burst, take the maximum shake and maximum hit_stop, never sum; one pause per burst, capped at 0.06 seconds and 6 px. At most 48 live particles; discard excess oldest particles. Clamp camera displacement, not gameplay positions.",
    "routing": "attack_heavy replaces attack_single/attack_all/enemy_attack visuals for an individual hit of at least 20 resolved damage; for multi-target hits apply threshold per target and merge feedback by burst. Emit at each resolved hit, never add heavy feedback to default attack feedback. overshield_gain replaces block_gain for Overshield. pointy_retaliation replaces default attack visuals for Pointy damage. pollen_tick replaces generic debuff visuals for periodic Pollen activation, with draw handled by game UI. waste_exhaust replaces generic exhaust visuals; its random-target damage separately emits attack_single. photosynthesis replaces energy_gain only for energy actually gained through Photosynthesis; do not infer new mechanics. For a power card, emit card_play_power once on the caster and status_buff only for additional recipients. A status application on an existing recipient uses the appropriate status trigger once.",
    "accessibility": "Reduced motion mode: set shake and hit_stop to zero, disable particle emission and rotation interpolation, halve peak alpha of additive sprites. Do not flash the full screen.",
